From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: d2d1: effects and device contexts as Paint.NET uses them

Paint.NET 5 draws its whole window with Direct2D, through its own effects
(ComputeSharp.D2D1 pixel shaders) and Direct2D's built-in ones. It stopped
at startup on one Direct2D gap after another:

 - Only 6 built-in effects were registered. All of Direct2D's 65 are now,
   with their properties' names, types and documented defaults in the order
   of their D2D1_*_PROP enumerations (the missing CLSIDs go into
   d2d1effects_2.idl). A built-in effect's properties are kept with the
   effect, so SetValue works on them (only system properties could be set);
   blob, string, IUnknown and color context values are stored and
   reference-counted; float and int32 initial values are parsed.
 - An effect factory returns the implementation's IUnknown, which need not
   be its ID2D1EffectImpl: a .NET ComWrappers object's is not, and Wine
   called Initialize through the IUnknown's vtable. It now QIs.
 - The effect context is an ID2D1EffectContext2 (new d2d1effectauthor_1.idl:
   ID2D1EffectContext1/2); GetMaximumSupportedFeatureLevel answers from the
   device; CreateTransformNodeFromEffect makes a node of an effect; transform
   graphs accept nodes that are not draw transforms; ID2D1DrawInfo keeps the
   output buffer, input descriptions, constant buffers and resource
   textures it is given; blend and border transforms take an output buffer.
 - Drawing swaps in a device context state; it was at feature level 10_0,
   which the device takes on meanwhile, so effects' shader model 5 shaders
   were refused. It is at the device's own level now. The device of WIC
   bitmap, DC and HWND render targets is created at the highest level there
   is (Windows draws those with WARP, 11_1), not 10_0.
 - Flush fails with D2DERR_WRONG_STATE outside BeginDraw/EndDraw (programs
   ask it whether they are drawing) and flushes inside; an empty command
   list closes; a command list set as the target mid-frame records.
 - Color contexts exist (sRGB and scRGB carry an ICC profile built from the
   sRGB standard's numbers; ICC, file, WIC, DXGI and simple ones); gradient
   stop collections are ID2D1GradientStopCollection1 (and the device
   context's CreateGradientStopCollection works); geometry realizations are
   made and drawn (as their geometry, filled or stroked).

Gate: test/d2dfx-gate.sh. d2d1:d2d1 0 failures (todo_wine removed where it
now passes: crop and blend/border SetOutputBuffer, closing an empty list).
